@* What a container's card says about it in words: its Id, its Status, its
   Ports, its Networks, when it was created, and on a line of its own its
   image's tag, with the version its image says it is when it says one. The card's body draws them
   beside its dials (ContainerCardBody); the dashboard's details object draws
   them alone, the dials being objects of their own. *@

<div class="wslc-card-texts">
    <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" title="@Container.Id"><b>Id</b> @Container.Id</MudText>
    <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" title="@Container.Status"><b>Status</b> @Container.Status</MudText>
    <MudText Typo="Typo.body2"><b>Ports</b> <PortsLink Ports="Container.Ports" Container="@Container.Id" Publications="Container.Published" /></MudText>
    <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" title="@Container.Networks"><b>Networks</b> @Readings.Dash(Container.Networks)</MudText>
    @* When it was made, and the version it runs on a line of its own, always: a patched image's tag and the
       version it says it is did not fit beside it. Each one line, as every line here is, cut where the card
       ends and whole in its title. Blocks, as the lines above are: MudBlazor draws a caption as a span,
       which no width holds, and it ran out of the card. *@
    <MudText Typo="Typo.caption" Class="mud-text-secondary d-block" title="@Container.CreatedAt">Created @Readings.Age(Container.CreatedAt, Container.RunningFor)</MudText>
    <MudText Typo="Typo.caption" Class="mud-text-secondary d-block" title="@Version">@Version</MudText>
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ContainerSummary Container { get; set; } = default!;

    /// <summary>Its image's tag, and the version the image says it is when it says one the tag does not (<c>latest (1.23)</c>).</summary>
    private string Version => ImageVersionText.WithTag(ImageReference.Split(Container.Image).Tag, Container.ImageVersion, Container.ImageVersionFrom);
}
